# C-type dipole yoke -- half model (Z symmetry), HEX yoke + tet air
# Canonical geometry: ELF CEFC 2020 C-Type model (yoke.jou -> yoke.step),
# mirrored about x=0 to recover full depth so the Add Kelvin launcher
# can reduce only the single (z>=0) half and use the IH-style zplane
# seam to copy the air sphere mesh onto the Kelvin exterior 1:1.
# Units: meters
#
# Coordinate system:
#   y = gap direction (pole tip at y~0, main leg at y~0.15)
#   z = beam direction (symmetry at z=0)
#   x = depth/thickness (full width, no symmetry)
#
# Symmetry planes: z=0 only (quarter-model x=0 symmetry was dropped
#   because Cubit's copy-mesh couldn't copy a 1/4-sphere surface onto
#   the Kelvin exterior; half-z works reliably -- same pattern as the
#   IH FEM-Kelvin samples).
# Use "Half (Z)" in Add Kelvin dialog  (auto-detect picks this up).
#
# 3 volumes (NOT united) for structured hex meshing:
#   Vol 1: Pole piece   (near gap)
#   Vol 2: Yoke back    (horizontal return)
#   Vol 3: Main leg     (coil location)
reset

# === Pole piece (near gap) ===
# ELF: 40mm(y) x 100mm(z) x 25mm(x) - full depth
brick x 0.025 y 0.040 z 0.050
move volume 1 x 0 y 0.020 z 0.025

# === Yoke back (horizontal return) ===
# ELF: 80mm(y) x 50mm(z) x 25mm(x)
brick x 0.025 y 0.080 z 0.025
move volume 2 x 0 y 0.080 z 0.0125

# === Main leg (where coil sits) ===
# ELF: 62.5mm(y) x 105mm(z) x 25mm(x)
brick x 0.025 y 0.0625 z 0.0525
move volume 3 x 0 y 0.15125 z 0.02625

# === Imprint/merge for shared surfaces (continuous mesh) ===
imprint volume all
merge volume all

# === Hex mesh ===
volume all scheme map
volume 1 size 0.005
volume 2 size 0.008
volume 3 size 0.006
mesh volume all

# === Air domain for FEM (tet mesh) ===
# Half-z model: air = upper hemisphere (z>=0).  Same pattern as the
# IH FEM-Kelvin samples -- Add Kelvin copies the hemisphere surface
# mesh onto a Kelvin exterior hemisphere 1:1.  The zplane webcut
# creates an equator seam curve for the copy.
create sphere radius 0.40
webcut volume 4 with plane zplane
delete volume 5
# Subtract yoke from the upper hemisphere
subtract volume 1 2 3 from volume 4 keep
imprint volume all
merge volume all
volume 4 scheme tetmesh
volume 4 size 0.02
mesh volume 4

# === Blocks ===
set duplicate block elements on
block 1 add volume 1 2 3
block 1 name "yoke"
block 2 add volume 4
block 2 name "air"

# Kelvin (FEM only): add via the launcher dialog "Add Kelvin open
# boundary (auto)" checkbox with "Quarter (X,Z)" symmetry.  The
# launcher injects add_kelvin_cubit(symmetry=["x","z"]) via
# auto_kelvin_entry.py just before radia_export netgen.
